15 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Flowchart showing participant selection for a study on women scheduled for ultrasound-guided biopsies. Initially, 215 women were considered. Ninety-four were excluded for reasons such as benign results \(38\), ductal carcinoma in situ \(19\), small tumor size \(8\), non-mass lesions on MRI \(7\), refusal to participate \(10\), no MRI before treatment \(4\), inadequate volume histological imaging imaging \(3\), and use of a different MRI protocol \(5\). Finally, 121 women participated in the study.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (\(A\) MRI scan displaying an enhancing breast mass indicated by an arrow. \(B\) Same MRI scan of breast tumor marked by three-dimensional segmentation \(intratumoral region - red, peritumoral region - green\) \(C\) Microscopy images representing the expression of extracellular matrix components. \(D\) Microscopy images representing the abundance of immune cells.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating the radiomics workflow. It begins with segmentation of intratumoral and peritumoral regions on five MRI sequences \(diffusion weighted, precontrast T1, initial and delayed postcontrast T1, and T2 weighted images\). Feature extraction includes first-order, texture, shape and volume, and wavelet features. Radiomic features were selected, and model building was predicted using the least absolute shrinkage and selection operator \(LASSO\) and linear regression analysis. Model performance was evaluated using the area under the receiver-operating characteristic curve.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Two side-by-side ROC curve plots labeled A and B both depict the true positive rate versus the false positive rate. Colored lines indicate five-fold cross-validation folds, with shaded 95 % confidence intervals and a diagonal reference line. Plot A shows a mean AUC of 0.82 \(95 % CI 0.78\2050.87\), and Plot B shows a mean AUC of 0.82 \(95 % CI 0.78\2050.88\).  ) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Two ROC curve panels labeled A and B illustrate model performance. Each plot charts the true-positive rate on the vertical axis and the false-positive rate on the horizontal axis. Multiple colored curves correspond to five-fold cross-validation folds, and translucent shaded bands represent 95 % confidence intervals. Plot A achieved a mean AUC of 0.82 \(95 % CI 0.77\2050.87\), and Plot B reached 0.83 \(95 % CI 0.78\2050.88\).   ) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
